       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults of 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects. Raising the dose past 200 mg also hasn't been shown to work better.\n\nWas 400 mg intentional, or is it a typo? Here are some options:\n\n- **Standard maximum:** sertraline 200 mg PO once daily. Depending on whether the patient is already on it, I can enter a lower starting or titration dose instead, such as 50 mg daily.\n- **Intentional 400 mg:** if you want it for a specific reason, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's above the usual maximum and was intentional. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n\nTell me which you'd like and I'll enter it."
